  "goodToKnow": "Die Stadtmauer is a city wall. Several Bavarian towns still have complete medieval walls you can walk on, notably Rothenburg ob der Tauber and Nördlingen, whose round wall lies inside an ancient meteor crater, the Ries. Many cities replaced their walls with ring roads or parks in the 19th century, such as Vienna's Ringstraße. Die Mauer alone often means the Berlin Wall. Plural: die Stadtmauern."
